{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Verified -1 on change 1702, triaged and rechecked (not a defect in this change).\n\nFailure: tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py::test_heal_folds_into_the_ref_from_a_detached_head_tracker, ONE shard only (ubuntu-latest py3.11) out of four. git commit-tree aborted with 'error: unable to create temporary file: No such file or directory', so the doctor raised S3DoctorConflict folding a head into the published ref. ubuntu py3.12, ubuntu py3.13 and macos py3.13 all passed the identical code in the same run; all 9 tests in that file pass locally on this exact commit. A logic defect does not pick one interpreter.\n\nNot reachable from this diff: the change touches transition_close.py (deleting compact-on-close), docs/concurrency.md, CHANGELOG.md and three test files. Nothing in it reaches the s3 doctor. Note the integration tier is excluded from CI's main pytest invocation (-m 'not integration'), which is why my local run never exercised this test — worth remembering rather than treating the local run as complete coverage.\n\nThe signature is already documented as transient IN THIS REPO. event_append.py:183 defines _TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS including 'unable to create temporary file', and the comment at event_append.py:175 describes exactly this fault — the loose-object temp create under .git/objects/ returning ENOENT on Linux — as 'a transient filesystem hiccup, NOT a data fault — the identical add succeeds on retry (a Gerrit recheck on the same patchset passes)', recorded under bugs vocal-dip-robin / brainy-floral-globefish. The s3 doctor is separately known to attract this fault class: commit aa61323613 routed its _git through the self-healing seam after three CI failures of the same bundle step.\n\nSo the recheck is evidence-backed, not a shrug. Posted on 1702 with the full reasoning.\n\nDiscovered work, filed as unheedful-custodial-bluebottle (f7da-baae-3c93-47e2), linked discovered_from: the retry that recognises this signature (_with_transient_add_retry) is composed only into event_append._git_add. gitutil.run_git_write — which s3_doctor._git, compaction and the claim/transition writers all use — retries only READ-side signatures ('could not parse head', 'bad object'). A write-side temp-file ENOENT matches nothing there, so it aborts on the first attempt. One fault class, self-healed in one caller and fatal in every other. Deliberately NOT folded into this change: it is a different concern with its own blast radius and deserves its own review."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786601471039328001,"uuid":"4196e2a5-b534-43ef-9a79-3c470fe3ae86"}